s are the functors\n<MATH_0004>\nand\n<MATH_0005>\nwhich are left adjoint to <MATH_0006>. Thus\n<MATH_0007> is characterized by the fact that\n<MATH_0008>\nfunctorially, for any <MATH_0009> and\n<MATH_0010>. We similarly have\n<MATH_0011>\nfor <MATH_0012> and\n<MATH_0013>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6620c624723a1f9c2b9089ade77cbbb50b2cd72e3d7ed4ce93c3591b6c48559c", "unit_id": "tag:03Q0:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03PZ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f^{-1}\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0002": "\\begin{equation}\n\\label{equation-pullback}\nU/X\n\\longmapsto\n\\colim_{U \\to X \\times_Y V} \\mathcal{G}(V/Y)\n\\end{equation}", "MATH_0003": "$(V/Y, \\varphi : U/X \\to X \\times_Y V/X)$", "MATH_0004": "$u$", "MATH_0005": "$u_s = (u_p\\ )^\\#$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-functoriality-general}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sites-proposition-get-morphism}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{equation-functorial}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{sites-section-continuous-functors}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{sites-section-functoriality-PSh}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cf8a76105ef701bfee80d5cb442ca8e9e1057e9fb91095223311d5946de53052", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dd446d0206250048990b3b91985b6596f45ae597424870e446d314942e08de65", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIt is not trivial that such an adjoint exists.\nOn the other hand, it exists in a fairly general setting, see\nRemark <REF_0001>\nbelow. The general machinery shows that <MATH_0001>\nis the sheaf associated to the presheaf\n<MATH_0002>\nwhere the colimit is over the category of pairs\n<MATH_0003>.\nTo see this apply\nSites, Proposition <REF_0002>\nto the functor <MATH_0004> of Equation (<REF_0003>)\nand use the description of <MATH_0005> in\nSites, Sections <REF_0004> and\n<REF_0005>.\nWe will occasionally use this formula for the pullback\nin order to prove some of its basic properties.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:eb30b1039c12c7f8f60fed1087a799fe744c06a312afe60b6a7e5db456bf0e34", "unit_id": "tag:03PZ:prose-0002"}
